    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26815" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῑθύραμβος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ], ὁ,</span> metapl. acc. sg. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διθύραμβα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					86
				</span></i>
			:—<i>dithyramb,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Archil.
				77
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Epich.
				132
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				13.19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pherecr.
				145.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				700b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1342b7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pr.</u>
				918b18
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μιξοβόας δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					355
				</span></i>
			: metaph. of <i>bombastic language,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοσουτονὶ δ. ᾄσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Hp.Ma.</u>
					292c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκέτι πόρρω διθυράμβων φθέγγομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					238d
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> a name of
			Dionysus, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				526
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Philod.Scarph.
				1
			</span></i>:—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δῐθυραμβογενής</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.524
			</span></i>. (<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
			</span></i> is said to have written it <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῡθίραμβος</span> (<i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				85
			</span></i>)—as if from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῦθι
			ῥάμμα,</span> the cry of Bacchus when sewn up in his father's
			thigh.)</div>
